:'''Phainon:''' It is as the rumors said &mdash; the Sky Castrum was far from united.
:'''Hyacine:''' My guess was right. This venue is indeed where celestial rituals were performed. Memmie, can you retrieve even more memories?
:'''Mem:''' No problem at all. Here goes...
:'''Mem:''' ...There we are!
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|"Wind, snow, rain, shine..."}}
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|"In the name of the Sky's Hundred Eyes, I bring celestial phenomena upon the world."}}
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|"The turn of dawn and dusk, commanding the celestial globe..."}}
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|"Awaken, Celestial Mural..."}}
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' Stop, foolish Cloudborn!
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' How dare you tamper with the celestial globe and distort the weather? This is blasphemy!
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' ...The Titan bequeathed the celestial globe to our ancestors, so that we could divide the light and dark equally between day and night, so that all things could grow beneath the celestial phenomenon they preferred.
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' But the Sunborn have asserted control over the celestial mural, and now the days are endless, subjecting the land to drought and burning... And you have the gall to accuse the Rainfolk, who you've oppressed!?
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' The land? It is our eternal nemesis!
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' How can storm clouds and rain, unloved by Aquila, lead the Skyfolk to victory in the Chrysos War?
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' Your character is as weak as your faith... Go seek out a corner untouched by the sun, and weep solitary tears in the shadows. That's all you lot know how to do anyway &mdash; cry in silence!
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' Hmph... Then let us show you what we are really made of...
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' You... What are you...
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' What are you trying to do?
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' Fanatics whose minds have been muddled by the heat...
:'''Past Rainfolk:''' By Aquila above, meet your demise!
:'''Past Sunfolk:''' ...Uwoahhhhhhh!!!
:'''Mem:''' Ugh... Ah... What a terrifying memory...
:'''Phainon:''' The brutal internal strife is sad to see... It appears the Sky cities didn't fall to external threats after all.
:'''Hyacine:''' The proud Sunfolk saw themselves as divinely chosen, exacting long-standing oppression on other tribes... And the Rainfolk suffering beneath them began resenting the divine, and plotted their retaliation.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} A common story everywhere...
::'''Dan Heng:''' The divine set the stage, and the mortals perform the play. This isn't the first time we've witnessed such a scene while trailblazing.
::People are truly ignorant.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Not surprising when living in a world with literal gods that you can see.
::This blame lies squarely on the Titan's shoulders.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} People are truly ignorant.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Not surprising when living in a world with literal gods that you can see.
::This blame lies squarely on the Titan's shoulders.
